  "description": "AMUNAA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H78 Cl4 Gd8 N28 O16,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 3 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 3 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 3 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.753-3.901 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.11-111.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C90H122Cl4Gd8N32O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies S(I).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
